{"id": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE-R002", "action": "retire", "frozen": [], "retired_reason": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE-R038.1 owns the run-side recall and seal of episodes; MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R155 owns episode grouping.", "new_children": [], "new_rows_requested": [], "cross_edits_requested": [{"row": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE-R038.1", "change": "Add the refusal `episode_revision_stale` for a transcript revision that differs from the recalled episode, and pass the engine code EPISODE_ORDER_UNKNOWN through for a conflicting chronology."}, {"row": "MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R155.3", "change": "When the caller sends no EpisodeSpec, MemoryRemember groups transcript turns into episodes by knob episodes.gap (default 30 min, range [1 min, 1440 min], Tunable). Layers are procedural for tool turns, semantic for extracted facts and episodic for the rest. The episode digest covers session id, first turn id and last turn id."}], "decisions": ["The old pinned name episode-gap-v1 carried a version suffix; the value becomes knob episodes.gap owned by medulla."], "consumer_notes": []}
{"id": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE-R003", "action": "rewrite", "frozen": [], "retired_reason": "", "new_children": [], "new_rows_requested": [], "cross_edits_requested": [], "decisions": ["Consumer rows reuse the engine port, replay fixtures and RunLifecycle hooks that groups w13 and w36 define; the same NEW rows are repeated here so the apply step dedupes them by title.", "MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R106.2 is retired; the council consumer cites MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R106.1.", "Meristem failure codes are lower snake case. Engine codes pass through unchanged.", "The dead MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE prefix becomes MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE in every row.", "No consumer row holds a threshold. Each names the medulla knob whose value arrives in the answer."], "consumer_notes": []}
