{"id": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE-R033", "action": "rewrite", "frozen": [], "retired_reason": "", "new_children": [], "new_rows_requested": [{"spec": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE", "title": "Extend the engine decision port with served reads and writes."}, {"spec": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE", "title": "Replay recorded engine answers for consumer run tests."}, {"spec": "MERISTEM-HARNESS-CYCLE", "title": "Run lifecycle hooks called from the run loop."}, {"spec": "ARBORA-HOST", "title": "Arbora binds the engine read and write methods to the decision port."}, {"spec": "MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE", "title": "Serve the champion pointer read."}], "cross_edits_requested": [{"row": "MERISTEM-SCM engine decision port row (group w13 NEW:1)", "change": "Name read/write extension of the same port (this group NEW:1); keep one EngineDecisionPort."}, {"row": "MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R168.3", "change": "Retired row: meristem rows now cite MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R168.1; no change needed beyond keeping the retirement."}, {"row": "MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE-R805.8", "change": "Reference the pointer read row (NEW:5) as the consumer read of the governed pointer store."}], "decisions": ["Meristem consumer rows reach the engine only through EngineDecisionPort; read/write are added by NEW:1 because decide/assemble/log/put_blob do not cover memory, span and fact reads.", "Lifecycle hooks in run_lifecycle.py (NEW:3) replace hosted_run.py as the home of consumer behaviors; hosted_run.py is only the client-only run seam.", "Each consumer is opt-in through HarnessConfig.consumers received from the host plan, so no default engine call exists.", "tests/run/ and tests/skills/ paths are replaced by tests/harness/, tests/graph/ and tests/rlm/ which exist.", "Skill candidate directories are written into the run workspace, not meristem/skills/ (that holds only the development skill).", "R168.3 is retired in medulla, so R052.1 cites R168.1 only. MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE prefix replaced by MEDULLA-DECISION-ENGINE.", "Entry point cited as meristem.graph.execute_graph (no meristem.api exists); fixtures replay recorded medulla answers (NEW:2).", "Local refusal codes are lowercase snake case; engine codes pass through unchanged."], "consumer_notes": []}
